{
  "id": "stage-6-vendor-approval-request",
  "name": "Vendor Approval Request",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The approval gate\n\nOne execution, one vendor. Daily Watch and Chase calls this once per actionable vendor rather than sending them all through one shared wait, because an n8n Wait node only ever pauses an execution once. This is the workflow n8n's own docs recommend for human-in-the-loop-per-item: give each item its own execution.\n\nNo approver address configured, so the run stores a config notice and emails nobody. That is a deliberate refusal, not a fallback.\n\nOtherwise the execution **pauses here** until a person clicks. The approver sees the vendor, the reason, the intended recipient, the upload destination, and the exact draft.\n\n**No response in 24 hours means it expires rather than sends.** Silence never results in mail going out.\n\nClicking approve releases this one specific email. It is not an approval of the vendor.",
        "height": 920,
        "width": 1520,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "cc000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000001",
      "name": "Note - 0001",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -80,
        -400
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Logged either way\n\n**Approved**, so sent from the office's own mailbox, then send time, recipient, body and follow-up date are recorded.\n**Declined**, so logged and nothing is sent.\n\nAfter two ignored requests the escalation pre-pass in Daily Watch and Chase hands the vendor to a person and pauses automated chasing. It will not email a vendor indefinitely.\n\nNote: `stage_6_outbound_test_mode` redirects real sends to a test address while it is true. Switch it off deliberately before live use.",
        "height": 700,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "cc000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000002",
      "name": "Note - 0002",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1500,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      },
      "id": "75000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000001",
      "name": "Vendor Approval Request Trigger",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "approval-channel-email",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.approval_channel }}",
              "rightValue": "email",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "approver-configured",
              "leftValue": "={{ Boolean($json.approver_email) }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "actual-recipient-configured",
              "leftValue": "={{ Boolean($json.actual_recipient) }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "73000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000005",
      "name": "Route Email Approval Configured",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        300,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "return $input.all().map((item) => ({\n  json: {\n    source: \"email\",\n    source_ref: \"stage-6-config:\" + item.json.issue_key,\n    original_filename: null,\n    notice_code: \"STAGE_6_CONFIG_NOTICE\",\n    severity: \"hard\",\n    message: item.json.approval_channel === \"telegram\"\n      ? \"Stage 6 Telegram approval was requested, but Telegram approval is not configured in the demo workflow.\"\n      : \"Stage 6 email approval cannot run until approver and actual recipient addresses are configured.\",\n    details: {\n      vendor_id: item.json.vendor_id,\n      vendor_legal_name: item.json.vendor_legal_name,\n      approval_channel: item.json.approval_channel,\n      approver_email: item.json.approver_email,\n      actual_recipient: item.json.actual_recipient,\n    },\n    raw_payload: item.json,\n  },\n}));"
      },
      "id": "73000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000006",
      "name": "Store Stage 6 Config Notice Payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        600,
        260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT stage_6_store_config_notice($1::jsonb) AS config_notice_result;",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "73000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000007",
      "name": "Store Stage 6 Config Notice",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        900,
        260
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "postgres": {
          "id": "Postgres account",
          "name": "Postgres account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "sendAndWait",
        "sendTo": "={{ $json.approver_email }}",
        "subject": "={{ $json.approval_subject }}",
        "message": "={{ $json.approval_message }}",
        "responseType": "approval",
        "approvalOptions": {
          "values": {
            "approvalType": "double",
            "approveLabel": "Approve",
            "disapproveLabel": "Decline",
            "buttonApprovalStyle": "primary",
            "buttonDisapprovalStyle": "secondary"
          }
        },
        "options": {
          "limitWaitTime": {
            "values": {
              "limitType": "afterTimeInterval",
              "resumeAmount": 24,
              "resumeUnit": "hours"
            }
          },
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "74000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000001",
      "name": "Gmail Approval - Send and Wait",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        600,
        -80
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "Gmail account",
          "name": "Gmail account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const approvalItems = $input.all();\nconst contextItems = $items(\"Vendor Approval Request Trigger\");\n\nreturn contextItems.map((item, index) => {\n  const approval = approvalItems[index]?.json || {};\n  const approved = approval?.data?.approved === true || approval?.approved === true || approval?.data?.approved === \"true\";\n  return {\n    json: {\n      ...item.json,\n      approval_response: approval,\n      approved,\n    },\n  };\n});"
      },
      "id": "74000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000002",
      "name": "Recover Approval Result Context",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        900,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "strict"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "approval-result-approved",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.approved }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "true",
                "singleValue": true
              }
            }
          ],
          "combinator": "and"
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "74000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000003",
      "name": "Route Approved Stage 6 Email",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        1200,
        -80
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "message",
        "operation": "send",
        "sendTo": "={{ $json.actual_recipient }}",
        "subject": "={{ $json.drafted_subject }}",
        "emailType": "html",
        "message": "={{ $json.drafted_body_html }}",
        "options": {
          "ccList": "={{ $json.send_mode === 'test_override' ? '' : ($json.cc_recipient || '') }}",
          "appendAttribution": false
        }
      },
      "id": "74000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000004",
      "name": "Gmail Send Approved Stage 6 Chase",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        1500,
        -200
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "Gmail account",
          "name": "Gmail account"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// $items(nodeName) returns every item that node ever produced, regardless of\n// which branch of a later IF node they went down. Looking context up from\n// \"Recover Approval Result Context\" pulled back items that were never\n// actually approved and never reached this node, and paired them with\n// send_response by array index against sendItems, a shorter array of only the\n// truly-sent items. That silently marked declined vendors as sent in\n// outreach_log. Source context from the IF node's own true-branch output\n// instead (output index 0), which only ever contains items that took this\n// path, so it lines up 1:1 with sendItems by construction, not by luck.\nconst sendItems = $input.all();\nconst approvalItems = $items(\"Route Approved Stage 6 Email\", 0, 0);\n\nreturn sendItems.map((item, index) => ({\n  json: {\n    outreach_id: approvalItems[index]?.json.outreach_id,\n    actual_recipient: approvalItems[index]?.json.actual_recipient,\n    follow_up_days: approvalItems[index]?.json.follow_up_days,\n    approval_response: approvalItems[index]?.json.approval_response || {},\n    send_response: item.json || {},\n  },\n}));"
      },
      "id": "74000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000005",
      "name": "Build Sent Outreach Log Payload",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        1800,
        -200
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "executeQuery",
        "query": "SELECT stage_6_mark_outreach_sent($1::jsonb) AS sent_result;",
        "options": {
          "queryReplacement": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}"
        }
      },
      "id": "74000000-0000-4600-8600-000000000006",
      "name": "Mark Outreach Sent",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.postgres",
      "typeVersion": 2.6,
      "position": [
        2100,
        -200
